{"created": "2026-09-27T07:59:44.858561+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-06T13:08:02.651034+00:00", "id": 22991227, "conceptrecid": "22991226", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22991227", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22991226", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22991227", "metadata": {"title": "Number of subsets of Z/nZ closed under negation and doubling: terms to n = 200 and program", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22991227", "publication_date": "2026-09-27", "description": "<p>a(n) is the number of subsets S of Z/nZ such that S = &minus;S and 2S &sube; S &mdash; equivalently, the number of subsets of the levels {0, &hellip;, &lfloor;n/2&rfloor;} closed under j \u21a6 min(2j mod n, n &minus; 2j mod n). First terms: 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 9, 4, 7, 8, 15, 4, 24, 4, 27, 16, 28, 8, 81, 4, 104, &hellip; For odd n, a(n) = 2^k with k the number of orbits of \u27e8x \u21a6 2x, x \u21a6 &minus;x\u27e9 on Z/nZ; for even n the functional graph carries trees rooted at 0 and, when 3 | n, at n/3, and is a forest exactly when n = 2^a or 3&middot;2^a.</p>\n<p>Files. b400466.txt: n and a(n) for n = 1..200 (OEIS b-file format). a400466.py: the tree formula over the functional graph, a brute-force check for n &le; 20, and the b-file generator.</p>\n<p>Origin. The sequence counts the sub-vocabularies of the axis construction of a 12 &times; 12 Jacquard pattern system, where the doubling of a line's offset from the centre is the generating operation (companion notes, doi:10.5281/zenodo.22965031; One Object, Three Descriptions, doi:10.5281/zenodo.22986529); there n = 12.</p>\n<p>Licences. Data: CC BY 4.0. Code: AGPL v3.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Amiot, Anibal Edelberto", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0002-6414-9448"}], "keywords": ["OEIS", "A400466", "integer sequence", "doubling map", "cyclic group", "closed subsets", "Jacquard weaving", "combinatorics"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://oeis.org/A400466", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22965031", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22966838", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22945021", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "publication-report", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "Q141191562"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22991226"}}]}}, "title": "Number of subsets of Z/nZ closed under negation and doubling: terms to n = 200 and program", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22991227", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22991227?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22991227", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22991227", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22991227", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991226", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22991226", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22991226", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22991226", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22991227/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22991227/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22991227/versions/latest", "latest_html":